# Lending service rules

These rules apply to everything under `lending/`. The backend conventions in the
repository root still apply, this file adds the lending specific parts.

## Loan state

- A loan has exactly one status at a time. Read it from `LoanRepository`, never
  from a value the caller passed in.
- Funds only move for a loan in `APPROVED` status. Check the status first, then
  transfer, then record the new status. Never the other way round.
- Status transitions are recorded with an audit event that names the old and the
  new status.

## Amounts

- Principal, interest, fees and repayments are all `Money`. Never `Double`.
- Interest and fee rates are `BigDecimal` with an explicit `RoundingMode` at the
  point of multiplication.

## Structure

- Constructor injection. Services depend on `LoanRepository`, `TransferService`,
  `AuditLogger` and `RedactingLogger` through their interfaces.
- Public methods on `LoanDisbursementService` and `RepaymentService` return a
  sealed result type. A caller must not be able to ignore a failure.
- No `println`. Customer identifiers and amounts go through `RedactingLogger`.

## Tests

- Every disbursement or repayment path gets a JUnit 5 test, including the rejected
  path for a loan that is not approved.
